   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the New York state thruway authority to convey real property to Rye Country Day School",
    "basePrintNo": "S6590",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6590-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "General Services, Commissioner of",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6590\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act authorizing the New York state thruway\nauthority to convey real property to Rye Country Day School\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nTo transfer certain land owned by the New York State Thruway Authority\nto the not-for-profit Rye Country Day School to be used for recreation\nand educational purposes as part of a public/not- for-profit\npartnership between the City of Rye and the school.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1. Sets forth the intent and purpose of the act to transfer\nthis surplus property to the School for the property to be used on a\nshared basis by school and the city of Rye as specified in a\nmanagement and use agreement by the two entities. Section 1 notes the\nlong history of the City and the School in seeking recreational use of\nthe property since the 1980's.\n\nSection 2. Authorizes the Thruway Authority to transfer the property,\ndeemed surplus by the authority, to the School for fair market value.\n\nSection 3. The lands to be conveyed pursuant to this act are described\nin this section.\n\nSection 4. The City of Rye and Rye Country Day School shall enter into\nan agreement stipulating the future use of the facilities, which shall\nbe executed prior to the conveyance of land authorized pursuant to\nthis act.\n\nSection 5. In the event that the land described in section three of\nthis act shall cease to be developed as described in section one of\nthis act, such lands and any improvements thereon shall revert to the\nThruway Authority and the conveyance of a sum equal to the fair market\nvalue as determined pursuant to section two of this act shall be\nreturned to the Rye Country Day School.\n\nSection 6. Effective date\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe City of Rye and Rye Country Day School, a not-for-profit entity\nunder the laws of New York State, have sought to promote uses on the\nparcel consistent with community needs since the late 1980's, and have\npursued shared partnership use of the property for recreational\npurposes in various forms since the 1990's including discussions with\nthe Thruway Authority by both entities. Such uses were included in the\n2000 City of Rye Recreation Master Plan. The City and the Thruway\nAuthority agreed on a lease arrangement for recreation purposes in\n2009 and the Thruway Authority has since determined that the property\nis surplus and intends to sell the parcel.\n\nIn the fall of 2016, the City of Rye requested that the Thruway\nAuthority sell the parcel to the school as the best way to accomplish\nthe goals of the public/not-for-profit recreation partnership for the\ncommunity. Rye Country Day School has committed to build a\nrecreational playing field, track and field house to be used by the\nnot-for-profit and the public through the City of Rye on a shared\nbasis as specified in a management and use agreement by the city and\nthe school.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nThe Thruway Authority will receive full value for the parcel. An\nindependent appraisal has also been conducted.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
